# Secrets and identity material. These are provided at runtime by the bind
# mount, never baked into an image layer -- aura_signing_key.pem is the Ed25519
# key that makes her identity unforgeable, and .env holds the bearer secret,
# the Gemini key and the Telegram bot token. An image carrying these leaks all
# of them to anyone who can pull or inspect it.
.env
*.pem
proof_of_identity.txt

# Runtime state, not build input. The live database is bind-mounted; a copy
# baked into the image would silently diverge from it.
aura_memory.db
aura_memory.db-journal
aura_memory.db-wal
aura_memory.db-shm

# Build noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.gitignore

# Superseded
OLD_telegram_bot.py
